  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Management and engineering service contract (MESC) III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Focus on providing technical assistance and capacity building to Jordanian water utilities. The contract, which has a five-year performance period, aims to reduce non-revenue water (NRW) losses in Jordan, which currently account for almost half of the country&apos;s limited water resources. Under the contract, Engicon will oversee implementing and monitoring government-to-government grants, review infrastructure planning and design, monitor construction contractors, and provide administrative support to water utilities including Miyahuna, Aqaba Water Company, and Yarmouk Water Company.</narrative>
  </description>
